```json
{
  "function_call": {
    "name": "...",
    "arguments": "{...}"
  }
}
```

Where arguments is a JSON-formatted string. But many frameworks accept simpler form. We'll follow instructions strictly: Provide top-level key function_call with nested name and arguments (string). So we need to encode arguments as JSON string.

Thus:

```json
{
  "function_call": {
    "name": "authenticate_travel",
    "arguments": "{\"client_id\":\"my_client_id\",\"client_secret\":\"my_client_secret\",\"refresh_token\":\"my_refresh_token\",\"grant_type\":\"read_write\",\"user_first_name\":\"Michael\",\"user_last_name\":\"Thompson\"}"
  }
}
```

Yes. Ensure proper escaping. Also ensure quotes around keys etc. That's fine.

